  "domain": "facts",
  "title": "D006: Three-phase STATCOM -> regulated DC-link + bipolar AC",
  "routing": "behavior+structure+scenarios",
  "prompt": "Build a three-phase shunt STATCOM for a 400 V line-to-line, 50 Hz system. A three-phase grid and load must share a common PCC, and a controllable three-phase voltage-source converter with DC-link energy storage must connect in shunt at that PCC through one coupling reactor per phase. Read Vsrc_LL and P_load from base-workspace variables; their nominal values are 400 V and 10000 W, and each operates over a +/-10% envelope. The converter must keep its measured DC-link voltage near 700 V as the grid voltage and load vary, while exchanging predominantly reactive compensation current with the PCC. The DC-link regulation and reactive compensation must establish promptly after startup. Log Timeseries Vdc, Vac, Igrid and Icomp. Vdc must be the physical DC-link voltage; Vac must be one physical PCC phase voltage; Igrid and Icomp must be the corresponding physical grid and converter-branch currents.",
